Preserve pointer arguments passed through the stream ioctl protocol.

MicroPython's stream ioctl slot multiplexes integers and pointers through a uintptr_t argument.
On Capstone uintptr_t is 64 bits while pointers are 128-bit capabilities. mp_stream_seek converts
&seek_s to uintptr_t before the indirect call, so the caller passes it with scalar mv/sd/ld and
stringio_ioctl reconstructs an untagged address. Dereferencing it raises capability cause 24.

Make the carrier type port-configurable while keeping uintptr_t as the default. Conversion macros
name the integer and pointer edges explicitly. The Capstone port selects void *, so genuine pointer
arguments use the capability ABI while numeric requests travel as untagged carrier values and are
converted back before arithmetic.

Measured on the pinned EXTRA+MPZ domain: io_bytesio_ext.py, io_stringio1.py and
io_stringio_base.py change from FAULT to PASS; adjacent io_bytesio_ext2.py remains PASS and
io_iobase.py retains its pre-existing ordinary output mismatch. Emitted code passes seek_s with
ldc/stc instead of mv/sd/ld.

